[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi. I know that the uparrows for coercions are often useful to disambiguate the expression, but sometimes the expressions are not ambiguous to start with and too many uparrows make the syntax unreadable. E.g. from my development:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↑↑</span><span class=\"n\">τₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+ₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">νₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)(</span><span class=\"bp\">↑↑</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">․↑↑↑</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|ₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)[</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">․</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">↑↑</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">․</span><span class=\"mi\">𝟎</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+ₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↑↑↑</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+ₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">νₚ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">↑↑</span><span class=\"n\">τₚ</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there a way to completely hide them without tampering too much with Lean code?</p>",
        "id": 597685084,
        "sender_full_name": "Claudio Sacerdoti Coen",
        "timestamp": 1779742440
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you format it with <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib/wiki/Code-in-backticks\">#backticks</a>?<br>\nYou could try <code>set_option pp.coercions false in</code> to hide the arrows, but it'll add other stuff, wdyt?</p>",
        "id": 597686679,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779743384
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Setting pp.coercions false puts back all the coercions that I want to hide completely</p>",
        "id": 597686887,
        "sender_full_name": "Claudio Sacerdoti Coen",
        "timestamp": 1779743497
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This works: for every coercion, instead of using the coe attribute, I can write an unexpander.<br>\nThat's not easy to revert locally in case I need to see where the coercions are,  but I can try living with that and see:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pfx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Proc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pfx_nil</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- attribute [coe] pfx_nil</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrettyPrinter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">app_unexpander</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pfx_nil</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unexpPfxNil</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unexpander</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$_</span><span class=\"n\">myid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">throw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">()</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 597689383,
        "sender_full_name": "Claudio Sacerdoti Coen",
        "timestamp": 1779744632
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This works without removing the <code>coe</code> attribute:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrettyPrinter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Delaborator</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">app_delab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delabNatCast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Delab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubExpr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getExpr</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">guard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getAppNumArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≥</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getAppArgsN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)[</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">]!</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e'</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 597689638,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779744840
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Okay I have no idea what I'm doing but it works, and for all coercions I think:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PrettyPrinter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Delaborator</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">delab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">app</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delabApp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Delab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubExpr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getExpr</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">declName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getAppFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failure</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getCoeFnInfo?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">declName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failure</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getAppNumArgs</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">guard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≥</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">numArgs</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">numArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">delabHead</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nargs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">numArgs</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">delabAppCore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nargs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">delabHead</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nargs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">unexpand</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">delabHead</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CoeFnInfo</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nargs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">insertExplicit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Delab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coeFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nargs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tagAppFns</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getPPOption</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getPPTagAppFns</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">SubExpr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">withNaryArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coercee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withOptionAtCurrPos</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`pp.tagAppFns</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tagAppFns</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">withAnnotateTermInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubExpr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">withNaryArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coercee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coeFun</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubExpr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">withNaryArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coercee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coeSort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SubExpr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">withNaryArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coercee</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">delab</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(I modified <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.PrettyPrinter.Delaborator.coeDelaborator#doc\">docs#Lean.PrettyPrinter.Delaborator.coeDelaborator</a>)</p>",
        "id": 597690131,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779745227
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, wow, thanks. The @[delab app] is indeed the key.</p>",
        "id": 597690338,
        "sender_full_name": "Claudio Sacerdoti Coen",
        "timestamp": 1779745394
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There are many <code>simp</code> lemmas whose conclusion is <code>^^x=^x</code> (sorry, on mobile) and if <code>simp</code> doesn't get rid of your double up-arrows then you might want to write some more of those lemmas.</p>",
        "id": 597694716,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1779748713
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In my case that long expression I posted is just syntax (i.e. a term inhabiting an algebraic data type for the syntax of a process algebra). All coercions are just constructors of the (nested) datatypes(*) and there is really nothing to simplify. Of course I could define abbreviations for chains of constructors, but  then they would interfere with pattern matching and similar stuff. Since I am experimenting with Aristotle, I would like to avoid making Aristotle's life harder.</p>\n<p>(*) this is also the reason why there is never any ambiguity and thus just hiding completely the coercions is fine.</p>",
        "id": 597695198,
        "sender_full_name": "Claudio Sacerdoti Coen",
        "timestamp": 1779749100
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The thing that I'm arguing could be simplified is that if there's a coercion from A to B and a coercion from B to C then maybe there could be (i.e. you could make) a coercion from A to C, and then two arrows become one. In mathlib this is the approach we take when there are multiple coercions around e.g. <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Sylow.coe_coe#doc\">docs#Sylow.coe_coe</a> but maybe your use case is different and you really want to keep track of the individual coercions.</p>",
        "id": 597695404,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1779749286
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, I understood what you meant. That's what I usually do too, for example when projecting out of structure that is itself projected out from another one, or when composing two injections between datatypes. In this case, however, I have (k1 (k2 x)) where the two k are constructors of the syntax; if I create an artificial  function k1k2 to write k1k2 x,  tactics that look for a constructor, etc. etc. may break, depending on how much upto-unfolding they know.  Moreover even leaving one uparrow everywhere would make the syntax (that is already quite dense) uglier.</p>\n<p>Thanks for the suggestion anyway, though!</p>",
        "id": 597695949,
        "sender_full_name": "Claudio Sacerdoti Coen",
        "timestamp": 1779749747
    }
]